# Doofus Adventure Game

A 3D Unity game built for the Hitwicket Game Developer assignment (**HW_2026_Test**).

Doofus is a cube who loves exploring green platforms called Pulpits. Pulpits don't last long — guide Doofus across as many as possible before he falls.

---

## How to Run

1. Open the project folder in **Unity Hub** (Unity 6.3 LTS or later).
2. Open `SampleScene`.
3. Press **Play**.
4. Click **Start** on the title screen.
5. Use **WASD** or **Arrow Keys** to move Doofus across the Pulpits.
6. Reach 50 successful landings to win, or fall to trigger Game Over — either way, hit **Retry / Play Again** to go again.

---

## Level Completion Status

### ✅ Level 1 — Character Movement and Platform Placement
- Doofus moves via WASD/Arrow keys, with movement **speed read directly from `DoofusDiary.json`** (`player_data.speed`).
- Pulpits spawn dynamically using JSON values:
  - `min_pulpit_destroy_time` / `max_pulpit_destroy_time` — each Pulpit's lifetime is randomized within this range
  - `pulpit_spawn_time` — the remaining-time threshold that triggers the next Pulpit to spawn, so a new one always appears **before** the old one disappears
- Only **2 Pulpits exist simultaneously** at any time, enforced in `PulpitSpawner.cs`.
- New Pulpits spawn **adjacent** (matching the 9x9 platform size) to the most recently placed Pulpit, in a **randomized direction**, and never overlap a currently active Pulpit.
- Doofus **falls** (via Rigidbody + gravity) if he's not standing on a Pulpit when it's destroyed, or if he walks off an edge — this ends the game.
- Pulpits **smoothly fade out** just before their exact JSON-specified expiry. This is a purely cosmetic layer — the underlying timer, collider, and destruction moment are untouched and still match the JSON exactly.
- Robust JSON handling: missing file, malformed JSON, or an inverted `min > max` range all fall back gracefully (defaults / auto-correction) instead of crashing.

### ✅ Level 2 — Scoring
- Score increases by exactly 1 each time Doofus successfully lands on a **new** Pulpit (tracked per-Pulpit via a `hasBeenScored` flag, so standing still or re-landing doesn't double-count).
- Live score shown on-screen during gameplay, with a small **pop/punch animation** each time it increases for satisfying visual feedback.
- Score resets to 0 automatically at the start of every new run.

### ✅ Level 3 — Start Screen and Game Over Screen
- **Start Screen**: shown on launch; gameplay and Pulpit spawning only begin once the player presses **Start**.
- **Game Over Screen**: appears the moment Doofus falls, displaying the final score, with a **Retry** button that cleanly reloads the game.
- **Win Screen** *(bonus, beyond the base requirement)*: reaching a score of **50** — matching the brief's own framing ("Doofus has set a challenge to walk on at least 50 Pulpits") — triggers a dedicated "You Won!" screen with the final score and a Play Again option.
- A central `GameManager` state machine (`StartMenu → Playing → GameOver / Won`) drives all screen transitions and gameplay enable/disable in one place.
- The Pulpit Spawner is fully state-aware: it only spawns while `Playing`, and immediately clears any remaining Pulpits and stops all activity the instant the game ends (Game Over or Win) — no background spawning after the run is over.

---

## Extra Features (beyond the 3 required levels)

- **Background music** with automatic looping playback, plus an in-game **Mute button** to toggle audio on/off at any time.
- **Dynamic camera follow** — the camera smoothly tracks Doofus from an angled, zoomed-out perspective so both the current and upcoming Pulpit stay visible.
- **Randomized Pulpit color palette** (varying shades of green) instead of a single flat color, adding visual variety while staying true to the brief's "green platforms" theme.
- **Platform-assist movement**: Pulpits subtly shift toward Doofus as he moves, tuned independently of the JSON's speed/timing values, to keep the tight timing window fair and winnable without ever altering the actual JSON-specified numbers.
- Clean singleton-based architecture (`ConfigLoader`, `ScoreManager`, `GameManager`) using `DontDestroyOnLoad`, so core systems persist correctly across restarts.

---

## Design Note: Difficulty

Doofus's speed (3), Pulpit spawn timing (2.5s), and true 9-unit Pulpit adjacency are used **exactly as specified** in `DoofusDiary.json` — none of these core values were changed to make the game artificially easier. At these values, crossing between Pulpits requires precise timing, which is intentional: the brief itself frames this as a genuine challenge ("walk on at least 50 Pulpits"). Rather than loosening the JSON-driven numbers, difficulty is balanced separately through the platform-assist movement feature described above, keeping the submission honest to the spec while still being winnable.

